@startgantt Convoy Timeline

title A worked example: the time rules around one convoy
caption Illustrative dates for a convoy departing 20 November 2026. Validity periods are UNVERIFIED and are configuration (D34, D37).

printscale weekly
Project starts 2026-09-01
saturday are open
sunday are open

-- Preparation --
[Donations received, boxes attested] starts 2026-09-01 and ends 2026-11-13
[Convoy planned: route, truck list, crew, bookings] starts 2026-10-01 and ends 2026-11-18
[Convoy Leader nominated] happens 2026-10-15
[Leader sees route point headers only] starts 2026-10-15 and ends 2026-11-05
[Leader may read addresses (14 days before departure)] starts 2026-11-06 and ends 2026-11-25
[Loads signed off] happens 2026-11-10

-- Declarations --
[ENS, ELO and GMR filed or recorded] starts 2026-11-11 and ends 2026-11-17
[Goods list code valid (about 90 days)] starts 2026-11-11 and lasts 90 days
[Customs declaration valid (about 30 days)] starts 2026-11-11 and lasts 30 days
[Warning: declaration expires in a week] starts 2026-12-04 and lasts 7 days
[Warning: goods-list code expires in a week] starts 2027-02-02 and lasts 7 days

-- Journey --
[Departure (blocking requirements hold)] happens 2026-11-20
[UK exit and France entry crossed: GMR, ENS, ELO closed] happens 2026-11-20
[Ukraine border crossed: goods lists closed] happens 2026-11-23
[Delivered and accepted] starts 2026-11-23 and ends 2026-11-25
[Arrived: vehicles handed over, leader address access ends] happens 2026-11-25
[Closed: report generated, still correctable] happens 2026-11-28

@endgantt
